    "statementMarkdown": "A monic polynomial $p(x)$ of degree $n\\ge2$ has exactly $n$ real roots, counted with multiplicity. We know that the coefficient of $x^n$ is 1, all the roots are less than or equal to 1, and $p(2)=3^n$. What values can $p(1)$ take?\n",
